what sort of info should be displayed if luck is revealed? let's assume
that luck is an integer on a scale of 0 to 10, should you get a hint like:
luck 6 (10)         or would you prefer
you are hopeful     ?
if a scale is chosen, clearly the extrema are identifiable but how do you
interpret the mid-values other than being non-extremum?
if you use messages then you'll see something like the following:
offensive
inadeqaute
hopeful
reconcilled
pleasing
more than lucky    .
these messages convey more meaningful information but lack the quantative
feel that some seem to desire. the messages info is somewhat already a
feature of the game but could get expanded into other useful areas.

perhaps all your attributes could get listed (optionally confirmable) in the
post-game wrap-up in gory quantitative detail. that couldn't hurt.

